h :answer/value "v=4.94" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19299/selection/fe152c55106930971342688fff17499d38cebb7862323d45b03bec8f2fb26a2c" :answer/id #uuid "44b22279-6dcb-59bf-a7ba-3358315d793c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v=8.36" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19299/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "30760418-7658-59ba-9f92-a5679d8b1f45" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-19299/selection/53235e7810a5e02bdb41401d2b68f8b3d81a0e6bea4e93c6c0d7a5d40a83d824" :answer-field/choices ["q-19299/selection/815d1f7ee0147fab4c69f061a7413cb3391f09c9754f828ddcd437a16174b171" "q-19299/selection/b715e954773a3eb6e6222cbf17eba85d557cb7bcb4d8927e528f0989712a61f1" "q-19299/selection/53235e7810a5e02bdb41401d2b68f8b3d81a0e6bea4e93c6c0d7a5d40a83d824" "q-19299/selection/6618585c35760c8b5c6027e05fb7812eb8797cbb1f3394bcca3dd505532c4fbc" "q-19299/selection/fe152c55106930971342688fff17499d38cebb7862323d45b03bec8f2fb26a2c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-19299" :question/id #uuid "59ea1544-758d-5928-bf3f-4995dd8b61f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-19299" :question/problem "The position $s(t)$ of a particle at time $t$ is given by \n\n$$\ns(t)=4{e}^{-t}+3{t}^{2}-2t+1,\\,t\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the velocity at time $t=2.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the velocity function by differentiating the position function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{e}^{-t}+3{t}^{2}-2t+1) \\\\  & =-4{e}^{-t}+6t-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the velocity at $t=2,$ we substitute $t=2$ into the velocity function above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(2) & =-4{e}^{-2}+6\\cdot 2-2 \\\\  & =-4{e}^{-2}+10 \\\\  & =9.458\\,658… \\\\  & ≈9.46\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-19299/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a1ec1379-ce50-53c7-b04d-3380676ebeb9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-19299"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-48904/selection/278293b1c54d23726fe113a8134a6def2bc817d543a088581c33a6197e1fa951" :answer/id #uuid "aca909dc-cf39-5ec5-989a-efcc5fa4807b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{s}_{0}=1\\,\\text{m},\\,{v}_{0}=6\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48904/selection/0b3c6235a7435c29836ddaf8fcd70fe144e945fc6fdb6ede69e11e8ec656adb3" :answer/id #uuid "aae6976b-c7cb-59d9-9da5-0b21a0b04a2b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{s}_{0}=4.5\\,\\text{m},\\,{v}_{0}=2.5\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48904/selection/321b58188c0befe44e5a629bfc79007b92e02dbdd788a87a6a9e72f371e670a3" :answer/id #uuid "3a85dc44-bfaf-573f-9ca5-dc1bed7a404e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{s}_{0}=4.5\\,\\text{m},\\,{v}_{0}=2\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48904/selection/ef99fb09b121bd48b0157ae584281b0f626314aba09286d7be42859b2e0bbb68" :answer/id #uuid "5812579f-0557-5dcc-b268-088a007bb112" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{s}_{0}=3\\,\\text{m},\\,{v}_{0}=6\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48904/selection/eacbf7ce0e9b02d25356693ca861fe4cee59c8d5b55d93b0fe0bd163fdb0adb4" :answer/id #uuid "150cf5ca-cb1d-50aa-bca3-7b46cefc606c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{s}_{0}=1\\,\\text{m},\\,{v}_{0}=2.5\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48904/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "722a5ef6-5a5d-5306-a4d6-dd16bc6e2b5c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-48904/selection/278293b1c54d23726fe113a8134a6def2bc817d543a088581c33a6197e1fa951" :answer-field/choices ["q-48904/selection/278293b1c54d23726fe113a8134a6def2bc817d543a088581c33a6197e1fa951" "q-48904/selection/0b3c6235a7435c29836ddaf8fcd70fe144e945fc6fdb6ede69e11e8ec656adb3" "q-48904/selection/321b58188c0befe44e5a629bfc79007b92e02dbdd788a87a6a9e72f371e670a3" "q-48904/selection/ef99fb09b121bd48b0157ae584281b0f626314aba09286d7be42859b2e0bbb68" "q-48904/selection/eacbf7ce0e9b02d25356693ca861fe4cee59c8d5b55d93b0fe0bd163fdb0adb4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-48904" :question/id #uuid "3ae77e72-b12e-5e34-a452-174b8e1e2c84" :question/math-academy-id "q-48904" :question/problem "The displacement $s$ (in meters) relative to a fixed origin $O$ of a particle moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis is given by the equation $s(t)=(2t+1)^{3}$, where $t$ is the time, measured in seconds. Find the position and velocity of the particle at the initial moment of time $t=0\\,\\text{s}.$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the initial position, we substitute $t=0$ it into the equation $s(t)=(2t+1)^{3}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}_{0} & =s(0) \\\\  & =(2\\cdot 0+1)^{3} \\\\  & ={1}^{3} \\\\  & =1\\,\\text{m}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the velocity function by differentiating the position function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}((2t+1)^{3}) \\\\  & =6(2t+1)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the velocity at $t=0\\,\\text{s},$ we substitute $t=0$ into the velocity function above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{0} & =v(0) \\\\  & =6(2\\cdot 0+1)^{2} \\\\  & =6(1)^{2} \\\\  & =6\\,\\text{m/s}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-48904/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a1ec1379-ce50-53c7-b04d-3380676ebeb9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-48904"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-336164/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "c80122c4-8bac-5417-8536-b22ccc9a0c3d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336164/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "17425342-593a-56f8-93f3-f392ea2b0883" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336164/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "2fd8bd22-1114-585f-936f-88b3f7bbaddc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-336164/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-336164/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-336164/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336164/field-2/90d20add8cb96e8c64098a828346ebe017aba0b86e7641e8b8fdcb66da470b39" :answer/id #uuid "3471abda-64e9-5f71-b054-85331592ce95" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9\\ln(3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336164/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "060f8d6c-0eb3-5f37-a967-1dea8ee34a03" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-336164/field-2/90d20add8cb96e8c64098a828346ebe017aba0b86e7641e8b8fdcb66da470b39" :answer-field/choices ["q-336164/field-2/90d20add8cb96e8c64098a828346ebe017aba0b86e7641e8b8fdcb66da470b39"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336164" :question/id #uuid "7080eac4-3fa8-5049-bbb4-7c6a19b7e3b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-336164" :question/problem "The displacement $s$ (in meters) relative to a fixed origin $O$ of a particle moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis is given by the equation $s(t)={3}^{3t+1}$, where $t$ is the time, measured in seconds. Find the position ${s}_{0}$ and velocity ${v}_{0}$ of the particle at the initial moment of time $t=0\\,\\text{s}.$\n\n${s}_{0}=$\n{{field-1}}$\\text{m}\\,\\text{and}\\,$\n\n${v}_{0}=$\n{{field-2}}$\\text{m/s}$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the initial position, we substitute $t=0$ it into the equation $s(t)={3}^{3t+1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}_{0} & =s(0) \\\\  & ={3}^{3(0)+1} \\\\  & =3\\,\\text{m}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the velocity function by differentiating the position function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({3}^{3t+1}) \\\\  & =3\\cdot {3}^{3t+1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3 \\\\  & ={3}^{3t+2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the velocity at $t=0\\,\\text{s},$ we substitute $t=0$ into the velocity function above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{0} & =v(0) \\\\  & ={3}^{3(0)+2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3 \\\\  & =9\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\,\\text{m/s}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-336164/field-1" "q-336164/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a1ec1379-ce50-53c7-b04d-3380676ebeb9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-336164"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-316032/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "d3d3f607-046a-5af8-be50-0a6370ebbbce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316032/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "68d81add-6401-51a8-8b81-5b150b5d0b4c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316032/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-316032/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316032" :question/id #uuid "af7ae399-6485-5d28-ab37-1f5218476981" :question/math-academy-id "q-316032" :question/problem "The displacement (in meters) of a particle moving in a straight line is given by the equation $s(t)=2{t}^{4}-3t+5$, where $t\\ge 0$ is measured in seconds. At how many seconds is the particle's velocity equal to $509\\,\\text{m/s}?$\n\n$t=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{s}$" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the velocity function by differentiating the position function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{4}-3t+5) \\\\  & =8{t}^{3}-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want to know when the velocity is $509\\,\\text{m/s}$, we substitute $v(t)=509$ into the equation above and solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}509 & =8{t}^{3}-3 \\\\ 512 & =8{t}^{3} \\\\ {t}^{3} & =\\frac{512}{8} \\\\ {t}^{3} & =64 \\\\ t & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity of the particle is $509\\,\\text{m/s}$ when $t=4\\,\\text{s}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-316032/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a1ec1379-ce50-53c7-b04d-3380676ebeb9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-316032"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-336142/field-1/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a" :answer/id #uuid "94bd6fda-9ce8-5416-a112-bf610ec7c40e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336142/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "0eba9b1a-d770-56ed-bbfb-7ba9e61b7fce" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-336142/field-1/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a" :answer-field/choices ["q-336142/field-1/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336142" :question/id #uuid "27791598-f71f-584c-a797-b3aabea9949a" :question/math-academy-id "q-336142" :question/problem "The position $x$ of a particle at time $t$ is given by \n\n$$\nx(t)={t}^{2}-24\\sqrt[3]{t},\\,t\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the velocity at time $t=8.$\n\n$v(8)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The velocity is the derivative of the position function $x(t)$ with respect to time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-24\\sqrt[3]{t}) \\\\  & =2t-24\\cdot \\frac{1}{3{(\\sqrt[3]{t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =2t-\\frac{8}{{(\\sqrt[3]{t})}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the velocity at $t=8,$ we substitute $t=8$ into the velocity function above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(8) & =2(8)-\\frac{8}{{(\\sqrt[3]{8})}^{2}} \\\\  & =16-2 \\\\  & =14\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-336142/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a1ec1379-ce50-53c7-b04d-3380676ebeb9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-336142"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-336192/field-1/830cec4f788030bb1de82fd836c9687c483ff9e37eb858ca93c5597ee410bcf6" :answer/id #uuid "13f7a0b1-57c1-504c-b552-46cd17455ea8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.47" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336192/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "1d1b1fc7-103b-534f-b174-c938159c03b0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-336192/field-1/830cec4f788030bb1de82fd836c9687c483ff9e37eb858ca93c5597ee410bcf6" :answer-field/choices ["q-336192/field-1/830cec4f788030bb1de82fd836c9687c483ff9e37eb858ca93c5597ee410bcf6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336192" :question/id #uuid "d180e225-c221-5fcc-927f-4690f3c81980" :question/math-academy-id "q-336192" :question/problem "The position $s(t)$ of a particle (in meters) at time $t$ seconds is given by \n\n$$\ns(t)={t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the speed of the particle when $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,\\text{s}.$ Round your answer to 2 decimal places.\n\nThe speed of the particle is approximately\n{{field-1}}$\\text{m/s}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the velocity function by differentiating the position function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t) \\\\  & =2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ the velocity is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-{(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the speed is $|-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}|=\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}≈2.47\\,\\text{m/s}$ to 2 decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-336192/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "45b380ed-1974-5876-8c88-a45773741b48"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-336192"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-336179/field-1/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer/id #uuid "2815aabf-2a7d-5318-86ea-f6ad5f62348c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336179/field-1/10293ac0295e0e79554137a949f5c5c46b9812dcc0a3ecb6349c4cb5e6acdff3" :answer/id #uuid "7ef93873-1c75-556e-927b-db158eddd8e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336179/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "a4995d30-41d9-5642-8cc0-c66b233eb511" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-336179/field-1/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer-field/choices ["q-336179/field-1/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" "q-336179/field-1/10293ac0295e0e79554137a949f5c5c46b9812dcc0a3ecb6349c4cb5e6acdff3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336179" :question/id #uuid "4a79c169-ce2a-5452-85f2-e8bf7b0b618c" :question/math-academy-id "q-336179" :question/problem "The position $s(t)$ of a particle (in meters) at time $t$ seconds is given by \n\n$$\ns(t)=6\\operatorname{ln}⁡t-3{t}^{2},\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the speed of the particle when $t=2\\,\\text{s}.$\n\nThe speed of the particle is \n{{field-1}}$\\text{m/s}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the velocity function by differentiating the position function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6\\operatorname{ln}⁡t-3{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{t}-6t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen $t=2,$ the velocity is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(2) & =\\frac{6}{2}-6(2) \\\\  & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the speed is $|-9|=9\\,\\text{m/s}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-336179/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "45b380ed-1974-5876-8c88-a45773741b48"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-336179"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-316062/field-1/12b7d840a997b0af25896f37c76d366155c72a970c1525c62ec119b69786f393" :answer/id #uuid "3688dadf-170e-530e-8642-0b0c5c2cde4c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316062/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "e6e6e912-713f-5f89-a785-223805dd4752" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316062/field-1/12b7d840a997b0af25896f37c76d366155c72a970c1525c62ec119b69786f393" :answer-field/choices ["q-316062/field-1/12b7d840a997b0af25896f37c76d366155c72a970c1525c62ec119b69786f393"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316062" :question/id #uuid "cadef097-386b-5352-9bf6-68f695d9a1ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-316062" :question/problem "The position $s(t)$ of a particle (in centimeters) at time $t$ minutes is given by \n\n$$\ns(t)=3{t}^{6}-2{t}^{4}-8{t}^{2}-7t,\\,t\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the speed of the particle when $t=1\\,\\text{min}.$\n\nThe speed of the particle is \n{{field-1}}$\\text{cm/min}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the velocity function by differentiating the position function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{6}-2{t}^{4}-8{t}^{2}-7t) \\\\  & =18{t}^{5}-8{t}^{3}-16t-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen $t=1,$ the velocity is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(1) & =18(1)^{5}-8(1)^{3}-16(1)-7 \\\\  & =18-8-16-7 \\\\  & =-13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the speed is $|-13|=13\\,\\text{cm/min}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-316062/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "45b380ed-1974-5876-8c88-a45773741b48"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-316062"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-109012/selection/9bc6a026ec1ca97c4b91621e1d722b108725fa0d077ed0b94ecca5ab1385fe2f" :answer/id #uuid "17390346-4487-530a-bc57-de1feaddd428" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{miles/h}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109012/selection/c3e61f1bd3a0e6452f92ced52f5eb3a80959f5881319f05ad6e29cecbb1c4480" :answer/id #uuid "335bf88d-0c9c-5da8-83c5-99e5c9c7cbea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1\\,\\text{miles/h}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109012/selection/2b1874c9c3a6edad61e901b3abf0fef52efd3f1a4c5be118975bac191a5cf444" :answer/id #uuid "bdd6723b-2976-54e8-ae1d-8ff9bbaca195" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\,\\text{miles/h}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109012/selection/9ead971751da2a6af82db8c99fcc9a1d5c7023f65185f738882d442f0003fb5d" :answer/id #uuid "516642fa-c839-5acb-9120-b0f3689b69fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}\\,\\text{miles/h}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109012/selection/9dcca324c996d5efd14a9bfe28f5e3d43a69eb05ae40228a20442770898dfc73" :answer/id #uuid "c72cc472-d884-5510-be50-be573d789ca5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}\\,\\text{miles/h}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109012/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "74f92c50-9db9-5edf-b81f-7ca1784d0f70" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-109012/selection/9bc6a026ec1ca97c4b91621e1d722b108725fa0d077ed0b94ecca5ab1385fe2f" :answer-field/choices ["q-109012/selection/9bc6a026ec1ca97c4b91621e1d722b108725fa0d077ed0b94ecca5ab1385fe2f" "q-109012/selection/c3e61f1bd3a0e6452f92ced52f5eb3a80959f5881319f05ad6e29cecbb1c4480" "q-109012/selection/2b1874c9c3a6edad61e901b3abf0fef52efd3f1a4c5be118975bac191a5cf444" "q-109012/selection/9ead971751da2a6af82db8c99fcc9a1d5c7023f65185f738882d442f0003fb5d" "q-109012/selection/9dcca324c996d5efd14a9bfe28f5e3d43a69eb05ae40228a20442770898dfc73"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109012" :question/id #uuid "d585be43-c802-5898-9f5b-2c2fe6d06f55" :question/math-academy-id "q-109012" :question/problem "The position $s(t)$ of a particle (in miles) at time $t$ hours is given by \n\n$$\ns(t)=\\frac{3}{t},\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the speed of the particle when $t=3\\,\\text{h}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the velocity function by differentiating the position function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{3}{t}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen $t=3,$ the velocity is\n\n$$\nv(3)=-\\frac{3}{{3}^{2}}=-\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the speed is $|-\\frac{1}{3}|=\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{miles/h}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-109012/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "45b380ed-1974-5876-8c88-a45773741b48"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109012"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-336174/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "0b486aff-d76a-5d91-8065-a12e977148b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336174/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "afad9354-c849-52c2-a675-1479eb3835f9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-336174/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-336174/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336174" :question/id #uuid "59089536-93bb-5aa0-adf3-fe2e1f5b2781" :question/math-academy-id "q-336174" :question/problem "The position $s(t)$ of a particle (in feet) at time $t$ minutes is given by \n\n$$\ns(t)=\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}},\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the speed of the particle when $t=1\\,\\text{min}.$\n\nThe speed of the particle is \n{{field-1}}$\\text{ft/min}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the velocity function by differentiating the position function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{{t}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen $t=1,$ the velocity is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(1) & =-\\frac{4}{{1}^{3}} \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the speed is $|-4|=4\\,\\text{ft/min}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-336174/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "45b380ed-1974-5876-8c88-a45773741b48"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-336174"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
